A||||3||Lisa 86 2m4||Dewwipe tool?||||5||
Z||000000||Lisa 86 2m4||12-30-2000||10:27 PM||||Are there any pictures of the dewwipe tool out there? I am in process of replacing my wipes now, and I'm thinking if I can see a picture of this tool maybe I can come up with one. Thanks if you do!!!<BR>Lisa||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||12-31-2000||09:28 AM||||The dew wipe tool looks like a 90 degree screw driver. Imagine a piece of flat stock 1/2" wide, 1/8" thick and 4" long. The tip of a screwdriver would be welded to one end perpendicular to the long axis. You would use it like a wrench. There are some made which have ratcheting action, too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lisa 86 2m4||12-31-2000||09:33 AM||||Yeah, ok, I think I can picture it. Thank you, Will!||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||12-31-2000||09:35 AM||||There is a picture on the "Tools" page at Rodney Dickman's site ( <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> )<P>I had a friend weld a cutoff phillips bit to a flat piece of steel and then wrapped the whole thing in electrical tape so it wouldn't scrape the window.  There are others on the forum who have used a small, cheap openend wrench with a phillips bit epoxied into the jaw of the wrench to do the same thing.  <p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
